=============================================================
  Joint Hypothesis Tests (Wald)
=============================================================

Error-correction term as a whole
  H0: alpha = 0
  Wald chi2(3) = 3.4428, p-value = 0.3283
  ! NOT A TEST: under H0, beta is unidentified (Davies).  Use -lrtest -bootstrap

Weak exogeneity, one variable at a time   [H0: row i of alpha = 0, chi2(1)]

invest (nabla Y2 block):
  H0: this variable does not adjust
  Wald chi2(1) = 0.7659, p-value = 0.3815
  Cannot reject H0 -> invest is weakly exogenous for B.

income (nabla Y2 block):
  H0: this variable does not adjust
  Wald chi2(1) = 2.6010, p-value = 0.1068
  Cannot reject H0 -> income is weakly exogenous for B.

cons (Y1 block):
  H0: this variable does not adjust
  Wald chi2(1) = 3.3575, p-value = 0.0669
  Cannot reject H0 -> cons is weakly exogenous for B.

Exclusion from the cointegrating relations   [H0: row i of beta_2 = 0, chi2(1)]
  only the 2 nabla Y2 variables can be excluded: beta = [I_r ; beta_2] normalises on Y1

invest:
  H0: row 1 of beta_2 = 0
  Wald chi2(1) = 0.5848, p-value = 0.4444
  Cannot reject H0 -> invest can be dropped from it.

income:
  H0: row 2 of beta_2 = 0
  Wald chi2(1) = 6.2504, p-value = 0.0124
  REJECT H0 -> income belongs in the long-run relation.

All of B2 jointly:
  H0: B2 = 0 (the relation involves only the Y1 block)
  Wald chi2(2) = 307.9614, p-value = 0.0000
  REJECT H0 -> the nabla Y2 block belongs in it.

Short-run dynamics   [Gamma on nabla Y, Theta on the innovations]
  ! statements about nabla Y, not about the levels: a variable can drive
    another's DIFFERENCES and still be tied to it only through ec

Joint significance of the last short-run lag, Gamma(1):
  H0: Gamma(last) = 0
  Wald chi2(9) = 34.1925, p-value = 0.0001
  REJECT H0 -> the last AR lag is significant.

All cross effects jointly:
  H0: every off-diagonal coefficient of Gamma and Theta = 0
  Wald chi2(6) = 13.2683, p-value = 0.0390
  REJECT H0 -> the cross structure earns its parameters.

D.invest: what the others do to it:
  H0: no other variable enters the equation of D.invest
  Wald chi2(2) = 0.4846, p-value = 0.7848
  Cannot reject H0 -> D.invest is not driven by the others.

D.invest: what it does to the others:
  H0: D.invest enters no other equation
  Wald chi2(2) = 7.1755, p-value = 0.0277
  REJECT H0 -> D.invest drives the others.

D.income: what the others do to it:
  H0: no other variable enters the equation of D.income
  Wald chi2(2) = 3.2572, p-value = 0.1962
  Cannot reject H0 -> D.income is not driven by the others.

D.income: what it does to the others:
  H0: D.income enters no other equation
  Wald chi2(2) = 4.9348, p-value = 0.0848
  Cannot reject H0 -> D.income does not drive the others.

D.cons: what the others do to it:
  H0: no other variable enters the equation of D.cons
  Wald chi2(2) = 5.5654, p-value = 0.0619
  Cannot reject H0 -> D.cons is not driven by the others.

D.cons: what it does to the others:
